+## Changed
+
+- `src/model/mod.rs`: `CREATE_TABLES` now creates all twelve tables with
+  TypeScript's column names and order. `write_read_model` inserts the nine
+  event tables' rows of every archived snapshot in the given order and the
+  `notices` rows of every archived and rejected snapshot by folder name.
+  `build_read_model` reads the trial labels first, then `read_history`, writes
+  them, and fills the label columns.
+- `src/model/event_rows.rs` (new): `pauses` and `recertifications` row
+  mapping, including the `attribution` entry and `source` rules.
+- `src/model/stream_rows.rs` (new): `focused_runs`, `mutation_picks` and
+  `mutation_survivors` row mapping with per-task position counters.
+- `src/model/trial_rows.rs` (new): `validator_runs`, `validator_findings` and
+  `link_findings` row mapping, with the five-string valid-finding rule.
+- `src/model/notice_rows.rs` (new): the plan-record and manifest `notices`
+  rows and the archived/rejected folder sort.
+- `src/model/labels.rs` (new): `TrialLabels`, `read_trial_labels` and
+  `apply_labels`, one `UPDATE ... SET label = ? WHERE id = ?` per label.
+- `src/model/insert.rs`, `insert_events.rs`, `insert_trial.rs` (new): the
+  SQLite inserts for all twelve tables.
+- `src/model/rows.rs`: `table_events`, `number` and `entry_string` helpers,
+  and `count_i64`/`len_i64` made `pub(super)`.
+- `src/model/error.rs`: the `ReadModelError::Labels` variant and its message.
+- `src/lib.rs`: re-exports `TrialLabels` and `read_trial_labels`.
+- `tests/read_model_history.rs` (new) and
+  `tests/read_model_history_edges.rs` (new): the nine-table comparison against
+  `tests/fixtures/history-rows/<table>.json`, the label assertions, the
+  malformed label file, and the edge cases the mutation check needs.
+
+## Deviated
+
+- The two label scenarios (`trial-labels` and `malformed-label-file`) share one
+  test function so the file fits the 250-line budget; it carries both `Covers:`
+  lines.
+- `tests/read_model_history_edges.rs` is a new test file holding the
+  mutation-supporting cases (notice sorting, the halts-0 manifest outcome, the
+  second focused run, invalid findings). The task's verify target only runs
+  `read_model_history.rs`, but the proposal verify and cargo-mutants run every
+  test target of the crate, which is what the mutation step needs. Keeping them
+  in `read_model_history.rs` would have pushed it over 250 lines.
+
+## Missing context
+
+- None.
